  user_input {
    user_response: "Create a complete, single-file interactive background component for a web application using React (or HTML5 Canvas + Vanilla JS) and Tailwind CSS.\n\n### 1. Canvas Environment & Solid Color\n- Base background: Solid deep midnight navy (#0b0d19).\n- STRICT NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS: \n  - DO NOT include grid lines, coordinate crosses, wireframes, or background matrices.\n  - DO NOT include star-dots, floating particles, or dust speckles.\n  - The canvas must be completely smooth and velvety.\n\n### 2. The Volumetric \"Light Beam\" Dynamics (Inspired by illuminate-toggle.webflow.io)\n- Origin point: Top-right corner of the viewport.\n- Structure: A soft, wide volumetric spotlight/cone projecting diagonally across the screen toward the bottom-left.\n- Gradient & Colors:\n  - Core / Highlight: Electric cyan (#00f2fe) blending smoothly into vibrant neon purple/violet (#8a2be2).\n  - Diffusion: Soft, organic falloff with heavy radial blurring and `mix-blend-mode: screen` (or WebGL/Canvas 2D radial gradient with feathered stops) so the edges feel atmospheric, like a soft stage light cutting through a dark room.\n  - No harsh linear borders; the beam must taper and dissolve completely into the #0b0d19 navy background.\n\n### 3. Fluidity & Interactivity\n- Gentle Idle Motion: The beam should have a subtle, slow breathing/undulating effect (slight scale or opacity drift via CSS keyframe or requestAnimationFrame) to keep the canvas feeling alive.\n- Mouse Reactivity: As the user moves their cursor across the viewport, the beam angle/pivot should subtly shift (a gentle parallax/sway of \302\2615 to 10 degrees) tracking cursor movement smoothly with dampening/interpolation.\n\n### 4. Interactive \"Illuminate\" Toggle Switch\n- Position: Fixed or absolute in the top-right corner over the light\'s origin.\n- Visual style: Minimalist, glassmorphic pill switch (`backdrop-blur-md`, subtle translucent border).\n- State: \n  - Default state is \"Dark Mode\" (the rich navy backdrop with the cyan/purple beam active).\n  - Toggling changes the beam intensity or toggles between the dark cosmic beam and an illuminated state, updating CSS custom variables smoothly.\n\nDeliver clean, production-ready code with all styles and scripts self-contained."
    items {
      text: "Create a complete, single-file interactive background component for a web application using React (or HTML5 Canvas + Vanilla JS) and Tailwind CSS.\n\n### 1. Canvas Environment & Solid Color\n- Base background: Solid deep midnight navy (#0b0d19).\n- STRICT NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS: \n  - DO NOT include grid lines, coordinate crosses, wireframes, or background matrices.\n  - DO NOT include star-dots, floating particles, or dust speckles.\n  - The canvas must be completely smooth and velvety.\n\n### 2. The Volumetric \"Light Beam\" Dynamics (Inspired by illuminate-toggle.webflow.io)\n- Origin point: Top-right corner of the viewport.\n- Structure: A soft, wide volumetric spotlight/cone projecting diagonally across the screen toward the bottom-left.\n- Gradient & Colors:\n  - Core / Highlight: Electric cyan (#00f2fe) blending smoothly into vibrant neon purple/violet (#8a2be2).\n  - Diffusion: Soft, organic falloff with heavy radial blurring and `mix-blend-mode: screen` (or WebGL/Canvas 2D radial gradient with feathered stops) so the edges feel atmospheric, like a soft stage light cutting through a dark room.\n  - No harsh linear borders; the beam must taper and dissolve completely into the #0b0d19 navy background.\n\n### 3. Fluidity & Interactivity\n- Gentle Idle Motion: The beam should have a subtle, slow breathing/undulating effect (slight scale or opacity drift via CSS keyframe or requestAnimationFrame) to keep the canvas feeling alive.\n- Mouse Reactivity: As the user moves their cursor across the viewport, the beam angle/pivot should subtly shift (a gentle parallax/sway of \302\2615 to 10 degrees) tracking cursor movement smoothly with dampening/interpolation.\n\n### 4. Interactive \"Illuminate\" Toggle Switch\n- Position: Fixed or absolute in the top-right corner over the light\'s origin.\n- Visual style: Minimalist, glassmorphic pill switch (`backdrop-blur-md`, subtle translucent border).\n- State: \n  - Default state is \"Dark Mode\" (the rich navy backdrop with the cyan/purple beam active).\n  - Toggling changes the beam intensity or toggles between the dark cosmic beam and an illuminated state, updating CSS custom variables smoothly.\n\nDeliver clean, production-ready code with all styles and scripts self-contained."
    }
  }
}
