  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Establishing the Baseline**\n\nI\'m starting by establishing the foundation: a deep midnight navy (#0b0d19) canvas background. This is the bedrock, the starting point. I\'m focusing on getting that solid color right, making it a strict negative space.\n\n\n**Defining the Visual Constraints**\n\nI\'ve established the parameters for the \"light beam\" element, steering clear of any distracting visual elements. The smooth, velvety canvas will be the backdrop. I\'m focusing on a volumetric spotlight originating from the top-right, flowing diagonally towards the bottom-left. The core will be electric cyan fading into neon purple/violet with an atmospheric diffusion. I\'m considering using radial blurring for a soft edge. The beam will have a gentle, breathing motion.\n\n\n**Refining the Interactivity**\n\nI\'m now integrating user interactivity. The light beam\'s angle will respond to cursor movement, creating a subtle parallax effect with dampening. I\'m also adding a minimalist toggle switch in the top-right, transitioning between a \"dark mode\" with the neon beam and an illuminated state. This toggle updates CSS variables for smooth visual changes. I\'m also checking SEO, and updating the `<head>` of the HTML to ensure proper representation on the web.\n\n\n"
