  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the React Challenge**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the initial prompt to nail down all the requirements. It looks like the core challenge is designing an interactive background element for a web app using React and Tailwind CSS, or alternatively, a Canvas/Vanilla JS combo. I am focusing on the key constraints of a single-file component.\n\n\n**Defining the Visual Concept**\n\nNow, I\'m solidifying the aesthetic specifics. I\'m going with a deep navy background, and I have refined the \"light beam\" concept. It\'s a volumetric spotlight originating from the top-right, transitioning from electric cyan to neon purple, with a soft, diffused falloff. The goal is a velvety, atmospheric feel, achieved through radial blurring and `mix-blend-mode: screen`. The beam should dissolve seamlessly into the darkness, with no harsh edges.\n\n\n**Refining the Interaction Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the interactive elements. I am adding a gentle idle motion to the light beam with subtle breathing. Also, I am planning mouse reactivity, to make the beam gently sway in response to cursor movement. Lastly, I\'m integrating a toggle switch (glassmorphic pill) in the top-right, allowing the user to toggle between \"Dark Mode\" and an illuminated state. I\'m focusing on smooth transitions using CSS variables.\n\n\n"
