  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the precise structure needed for the interactive background component, considering both React and HTML5 Canvas + Vanilla JS options as specified. I\'m focusing on creating a single-file solution that meets the requirements of the prompt and explores the advantages of each framework. I believe a clear structure is key.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Features**\n\nI\'ve established the core visual aspects, beginning with a deep navy background. I\'m prioritizing the volumetric \"light beam,\" originating top-right and cascading towards the bottom-left, inspired by the illuminate-toggle example. The spotlight will consist of electric cyan blending into neon purple, with radial blurring and \'screen\' blend mode for an atmospheric effect. I\'m focusing on smooth gradients with no hard edges and no extraneous elements as specified.\n\n\n**Refining Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on interactivity. I\'m planning gentle, idle motion for the light beam, using subtle scale or opacity shifts to create a breathing effect. User cursor movement will also affect the beam angle. The light beam\'s interactive toggle is also being finalized; it will be in the top-right corner, appearing minimalist with a glassmorphic style. Dark mode will be the default, and toggling will control the beam\'s intensity, smoothly updating CSS variables.\n\n\n**Calculating Beam Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now deep in the math, specifically the calculations for rendering the volumetric spotlight using Canvas 2D. I\'m nailing down the viewport size and origin coordinates, including the dynamic calculation from the toggle\'s bounding box. The target base angle from the origin to the bottom-left is calculated, ensuring a visually appealing beam. I\'m focusing on making sure the beam math is optimized for performance, and the code is easily understandable.\n\n\n**Calculating Interactive Effects**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive effects and am working through the implementation of mouse parallax sway, using normalized mouse coordinates to calculate `swayOffsetX` and `swayOffsetY` to adjust the `targetAngle`. I\'m incorporating smooth dampening with Lerp to achieve a natural feel, interpolating between `currentAngle`, `currentIntensity`, and `currentSpread`. To give the light beam subtle idle motion, I\'m integrating breathing effects using `Math.sin` to create undulation in both the angle and spread of the light. Now I\'m considering rendering the volumetric cone in Canvas 2D, keeping the velvety falloff in mind.\n\n\n**Implementing Volumetric Rendering**\n\nI\'m now implementing a multi-pass approach for the Canvas 2D spotlight. The first pass will be the wide ambient bloom. I\'m focusing on defining the radial gradient colors and spread, blending with \'screen\' mode and blurring for an atmospheric effect. The second pass will be the main volumetric cone. I\'m taking care to ensure a smooth falloff, avoiding hard boundaries. I\'m calculating the cone vertices with `p0`, `p1`, `p2`, `p3`.\n\n\n**Defining Beam Gradients**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the color gradients for the volumetric beam in Canvas 2D, as specified. I\'m focusing on a multi-pass approach, including a wide ambient bloom with an electric cyan core, transitioning to neon purple/violet at the outer edges. The filter blur is being handled in each pass to achieve the atmospheric effect. The intensity control is critical for the visual effect. I\'m also planning a high-luminance core and origin aperture.\n\n\n**Defining Ambient Illumination**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the ambient lighting, specifically the radial blooms. I\'m focusing on a multi-layered approach using Canvas 2D. The first pass will create a bright, hot spot, transitioning to electric cyan and then fading. The second layer will form an outer halo with purple and cyan, fading to transparency. I\'m also planning a soft wash on the bottom-left corner of the viewport, using a radial gradient of purple and cyan with a high blur to simulate light interaction with the corner of a room. I\'m also setting a base canvas background fill of `#0b0d19`, transitioning to `#101428` during the \'illuminated\' state, which also boosts beam intensity.\n\n\n**Verifying State Transitions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dynamic CSS variable updates. I\'ve confirmed smooth transitions for `--beam-intensity`, `--beam-core-color`, `--beam-mid-color`, and `--bg-navy`. The \"Dark Mode\" default uses a solid navy background, with the beam intensity at standard and a cyan-to-purple gradient. The CSS variables are updated to reflect this state, including `--origin-glow-opacity` and `--illuminate-state`. I\'m verifying the minimalist, glassmorphic toggle button is fixed in the top-right corner.\n\n\n**Designing Toggle Component**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on designing the interactive toggle, specifying a glassmorphic pill container and a glowing LED aperture for a physical feel, aligning perfectly with the beam\'s origin. The \"Illuminate\" text will be accompanied by an animated thumb switch. This toggle will support click and keyboard navigation as specified, using `Enter` and `Space`, and incorporating ARIA attributes. It will transition to the beam illumination when clicked. I\'m taking care to meet the constraints: no grids, crosses, wireframes, or any extraneous visual elements. All that is left to do is to verify the strict negative constraints and we should be set.\n\n\n**Finalizing Export and Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the component. I\'m focusing on exporting `VolumetricLightBeam` from `src/components/VolumetricLightBeam.tsx` to ensure reusability. I\'m also ensuring the App.tsx renders the component as specified. I\'m including the toggle, control bar/drawer, \"Copy Code\" button, and refined typography. The control bar will include preset color themes, sliders, and toggles as requested. I\'m making sure to keep it clean!\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1551517"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React, { useEffect, useRef, useState, useCallback } from \'react\';\\n\\nexport interface VolumetricLightBeamProps {\\n  /** Mode: \'dark\' (default cosmic beam) or \'illuminated\' (boosted radiant beam) */\\n  isIlluminated?: boolean;\\n  /** Primary core color (e.g. electric cyan #00f2fe) */\\n  coreColor?: string;\\n  /** Secondary gradient color (e.g. neon violet/purple #8a2be2) */\\n  secondaryColor?: string;\\n  /** Base canvas solid background color (default #0b0d19) */\\n  backgroundColor?: string;\\n  /** Multiplier for overall beam brightness/opacity (default 1.0) */\\n  intensityMultiplier?: number;\\n  /** Beam cone spread in degrees (default ~42\302\260) */\\n  spreadAngleDeg?: number;\\n  /** Parallax sway sensitivity in degrees (default 8\302\260) */\\n  maxSwayDeg?: number;\\n  /** Whether idle breathing motion is active (default true) */\\n  idleMotion?: boolean;\\n  /** Optional custom origin coordinates {x, y} in pixels. If omitted, uses top-right anchor */\\n  originOverride?: { x: number; y: number } | null;\\n  /** Callback notifying parent of the calculated light origin {x, y} */\\n  onOriginUpdate?: (origin: { x: number; y: number }) => void;\\n  /** Custom class name for container */\\n  className?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * VolumetricLightBeam\\n * \\n * High-performance, velvety smooth volumetric spotlight component.\\n * STRICT NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS HONORED:\\n * - NO grid lines, crosses, or matrices.\\n * - NO star-dots, floating particles, or dust speckles.\\n * - 100% continuous, organic, velvety light falloff cutting through solid #0b0d19 midnight navy.\\n */\\nexport const VolumetricLightBeam: React.FC<VolumetricLightBeamProps> = ({\\n  isIlluminated = false,\\n  coreColor = \'#00f2fe\',\\n  secondaryColor = \'#8a2be2\',\\n  backgroundColor = \'#0b0d19\',\\n  intensityMultiplier = 1.0,\\n  spreadAngleDeg = 42,\\n  maxSwayDeg = 8,\\n  idleMotion = true,\\n  originOverride = null,\\n  onOriginUpdate,\\n  className = \'\',\\n}) => {\\n  const canvasRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n  const animFrameRef = useRef<number | null>(null);\\n\\n  // Dynamic state tracked for dampening / interpolation (lerp)\\n  const stateRef = useRef({\\n    currentAngle: 2.45, // Radians pointing roughly toward bottom-left (~140 deg)\\n    targetAngle: 2.45,\\n    currentIntensity: isIlluminated ? 1.4 : 0.95,\\n    targetIntensity: isIlluminated ? 1.4 : 0.95,\\n    currentSpread: (spreadAngleDeg * Math.PI) / 180,\\n    targetSpread: (spreadAngleDeg * Math.PI) / 180,\\n    originX: 0,\\n    originY: 0,\\n    mouseNormX: 0.5,\\n    mouseNormY: 0.5,\\n    hasMouse: false,\\n    startTime: performance.now(),\\n  });\\n\\n  // Keep target spread & intensity updated when props change\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    stateRef.current.targetIntensity = (isIlluminated ? 1.4 : 0.95) * intensityMultiplier;\\n    stateRef.current.targetSpread = (spreadAngleDeg * Math.PI) / 180;\\n  }, [isIlluminated, intensityMultiplier, spreadAngleDeg]);\\n\\n  // Sync CSS custom properties on document element for smooth glassmorphism / ambient transitions\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const root = document.documentElement;\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-intensity\', String(isIlluminated ? 1.4 * intensityMultiplier : 0.95 * intensityMultiplier));\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-core-color\', coreColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-secondary-color\', secondaryColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--bg-navy\', backgroundColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--illuminate-state\', isIlluminated ? \'illuminated\' : \'dark\');\\n  }, [isIlluminated, coreColor, secondaryColor, backgroundColor, intensityMultiplier]);\\n\\n  // Handle cursor movement with smooth normalized coordinates\\n  const handlePointerMove = useCallback((e: MouseEvent | TouchEvent) => {\\n    const clientX = \'touches\' in e ? e.touches[0].clientX : e.clientX;\\n    const clientY = \'touches\' in e ? e.touches[0].clientY : e.clientY;\\n    const width = window.innerWidth;\\n    const height = window.innerHeight;\\n\\n    stateRef.current.mouseNormX = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, clientX / width));\\n    stateRef.current.mouseNormY = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, clientY / height));\\n    stateRef.current.hasMouse = true;\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const handlePointerLeave = useCallback(() => {\\n    // Gently reset to center when cursor leaves viewport\\n    stateRef.current.mouseNormX = 0.5;\\n    stateRef.current.mouseNormY = 0.5;\\n    stateRef.current.hasMouse = false;\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    window.addEventListener(\'pointermove\', handlePointerMove, { passive: true });\\n    document.addEventListener(\'mouseleave\', handlePointerLeave);\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'pointermove\', handlePointerMove);\\n      document.removeEventListener(\'mouseleave\', handlePointerLeave);\\n    };\\n  }, [handlePointerMove, handlePointerLeave]);\\n\\n  // Main high-performance render loop\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false });\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    let dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n\\n    const resize = () => {\\n      dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n      const width = window.innerWidth;\\n      const height = window.innerHeight;\\n\\n      canvas.width = Math.floor(width * dpr);\\n      canvas.height = Math.floor(height * dpr);\\n      canvas.style.width = `${width}px`;\\n      canvas.style.height = `${height}px`;\\n\\n      // Origin point: near the top-right corner where the illuminate switch sits\\n      const defaultOriginX = width - Math.max(64, width * 0.055);\\n      const defaultOriginY = Math.max(48, height * 0.055);\\n\\n      const ox = originOverride ? originOverride.x : defaultOriginX;\\n      const oy = originOverride ? originOverride.y : defaultOriginY;\\n\\n      stateRef.current.originX = ox;\\n      stateRef.current.originY = oy;\\n\\n      if (onOriginUpdate) {\\n        onOriginUpdate({ x: ox, y: oy });\\n      }\\n    };\\n\\n    resize();\\n    window.addEventListener(\'resize\', resize, { passive: true });\\n\\n    // Render step\\n    const render = (now: number) => {\\n      const state = stateRef.current;\\n      const time = (now - state.startTime) * 0.001;\\n      const width = canvas.width / dpr;\\n      const height = canvas.height / dpr;\\n\\n      // 1. Calculate natural base angle from origin toward bottom-left\\n      const targetPointX = width * 0.12;\\n      const targetPointY = height * 0.88;\\n      const baseAngle = Math.atan2(targetPointY - state.originY, targetPointX - state.originX);\\n\\n      // 2. Compute smooth mouse parallax sway (\302\261maxSwayDeg)\\n      const maxSwayRad = (maxSwayDeg * Math.PI) / 180;\\n      const mouseOffsetX = (state.mouseNormX - 0.5) * maxSwayRad * 1.6;\\n      const mouseOffsetY = (state.mouseNormY - 0.5) * maxSwayRad * 0.8;\\n\\n      // 3. Subtle, slow breathing/undulating effect\\n      const idleAngleDrift = idleMotion ? Math.sin(time * 0.6) * 0.035 : 0;\\n      const idleBreathingIntensity = idleMotion ? Math.sin(time * 0.9) * 0.06 : 0;\\n      const idleSpreadDrift = idleMotion ? Math.cos(time * 0.7) * 0.025 : 0;\\n\\n      // Target angle with mouse sway\\n      state.targetAngle = baseAngle + mouseOffsetX + mouseOffsetY + idleAngleDrift;\\n\\n      // 4. Smooth dampening / interpolation (exponential decay lerp)\\n      state.currentAngle += (state.targetAngle - state.currentAngle) * 0.06;\\n      state.currentIntensity += (state.targetIntensity - state.currentIntensity) * 0.08;\\n      state.currentSpread += (state.targetSpread - state.currentSpread) * 0.06;\\n\\n      const angle = state.currentAngle;\\n      const intensity = Math.max(0.05, state.currentIntensity * (1 + idleBreathingIntensity));\\n      const spread = Math.max(0.1, state.currentSpread + idleSpreadDrift);\\n      const halfSpread = spread / 2;\\n\\n      // Setup drawing transform for HiDPI\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\\n\\n      // 5. Solid velvety base background (deep midnight navy #0b0d19)\\n      // When illuminated, subtly lifts with a whisper of ambient navy luminescence\\n      if (isIlluminated) {\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#0e1122\';\\n      } else {\\n        ctx.fillStyle = backgroundColor;\\n      }\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\\n\\n      const ox = state.originX;\\n      const oy = state.originY;\\n      const reach = Math.hypot(width, height) * 1.45;\\n\\n      // Helper to draw a cone polygon sector\\n      const drawConePath = (coneHalfAngle: number) => {\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(ox, oy);\\n        const steps = 18;\\n        const startA = angle - coneHalfAngle;\\n        const endA = angle + coneHalfAngle;\\n        for (let i = 0; i <= steps; i++) {\\n          const a = startA + (endA - startA) * (i / steps);\\n          const px = ox + Math.cos(a) * reach;\\n          const py = oy + Math.sin(a) * reach;\\n          ctx.lineTo(px, py);\\n        }\\n        ctx.closePath();\\n      };\\n\\n      // PASS 1: Broad Velvety Ambient Fog / Bloom (Heavy Blur, soft atmospheric falloff)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(64px)\';\\n      }\\n      drawConePath(halfSpread * 1.6);\\n      const gradAmbient = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 10, ox, oy, reach * 0.95);\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(0.0, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.32 * intensity));\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(0.35, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.22 * intensity));\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(0.70, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.08 * intensity));\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(1.0, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradAmbient;\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 2: Main Volumetric Spotlight Body (Medium Blur, vibrant Electric Cyan into Neon Violet)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(30px)\';\\n      }\\n      drawConePath(halfSpread);\\n      const gradMain = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 5, ox, oy, reach * 0.85);\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.88 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.12, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.72 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.32, hexToRgba(\'#4f46e5\', 0.58 * intensity)); // Transition indigo\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.55, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.42 * intensity)); // Neon purple/violet\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.80, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.14 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradMain;\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 3: Core Intense Concentrated Beam (Tighter angle, sharp & luminous highlight)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(14px)\';\\n      }\\n      drawConePath(halfSpread * 0.45);\\n      const gradCore = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 0, ox, oy, reach * 0.65);\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(\'#ffffff\', 0.95 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.10, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.85 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.35, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.45 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.65, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.20 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradCore;\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 4: Stage Light Aperture / Emitter Glow (Point of origin near toggle switch)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(22px)\';\\n      }\\n      const apertureGlow = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 0, ox, oy, Math.min(220, width * 0.28));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(\'#ffffff\', 0.98 * intensity));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(0.15, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.75 * intensity));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(0.45, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.35 * intensity));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = apertureGlow;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(ox, oy, Math.min(220, width * 0.28), 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 5: Soft Atmospheric Floor Bounce (Bottom-Left Corner Wash)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(80px)\';\\n      }\\n      const bounceX = width * 0.12;\\n      const bounceY = height * 0.88;\\n      const bounceRad = Math.min(380, width * 0.38);\\n      const bounceGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(bounceX, bounceY, 0, bounceX, bounceY, bounceRad);\\n      bounceGrad.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.22 * intensity));\\n      bounceGrad.addColorStop(0.40, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.10 * intensity));\\n      bounceGrad.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = bounceGrad;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(bounceX, bounceY, bounceRad, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      animFrameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(render);\\n    };\\n\\n    animFrameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(render);\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'resize\', resize);\\n      if (animFrameRef.current) {\\n        cancelAnimationFrame(animFrameRef.current);\\n      }\\n    };\\n  }, [coreColor, secondaryColor, backgroundColor, maxSwayDeg, idleMotion, originOverride, onOriginUpdate, isIlluminated]);\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className={`fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none select-none overflow-hidden ${className}`}>\\n      <canvas\\n        ref={canvasRef}\\n        className=\\\"absolute inset-0 block w-full h-full\\\"\\n        style={{\\n          backgroundColor,\\n          mixBlendMode: \'normal\',\\n        }}\\n      />\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\\n\\n/**\\n * Utility helper to convert hex to rgba string\\n */\\nfunction hexToRgba(hex: string, alpha: number): string {\\n  let c = hex.trim();\\n  if (c.startsWith(\'#\')) {\\n    c = c.slice(1);\\n  }\\n  if (c.length === 3) {\\n    c = c.split(\'\').map((char) => char + char).join(\'\');\\n  }\\n  const num = parseInt(c, 16);\\n  if (isNaN(num)) {\\n    return `rgba(0, 242, 254, ${alpha})`;\\n  }\\n  const r = (num >> 16) & 255;\\n  const g = (num >> 8) & 255;\\n  const b = num & 255;\\n  return `rgba(${r}, ${g}, ${b}, ${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, alpha))})`;\\n}\\n\\nexport default VolumetricLightBeam;\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create single-file reusable VolumetricLightBeam canvas component\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/VolumetricLightBeam.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing component file\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create VolumetricLightBeam component\"}"
