  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Removing Mouse Tracking**\n\nI\'m removing the mouse tracking functionality in `VolumetricLightBeam.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m taking out `handlePointerMove` and `handlePointerLeave`, as well as the event listeners they manage. This also means deleting the related state variables like `mouseNormX`, `mouseNormY`, and `hasMouse`. This should streamline the component.\n\n\n**Fixing Light Beam**\n\nNow, I\'ve implemented a fixed light beam. The angle is static, pointing towards the bottom-left. I\'ve retained a touch of \"breathing\" and idle spread drift for a subtle, natural feel. I\'m focusing next on adding the particle system.\n\n\n**Adding Particle System**\n\nI\'m now integrating the particle system, aiming for an ethereal cosmic dust appearance. I\'m targeting 80-120 particles for an optimal balance of elegance and visual interest. Each particle will drift upward with a bit of horizontal sway, looping to the bottom when it leaves the view, and I\'ll include a twinkling effect. I\'m currently working on making the particles catch the light of the beam.\n\n\n**Calculating Beam Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how particles interact with the light beam, calculating the difference in angle between the particle and the beam itself, and normalizing it. I\'m also determining how to test whether a particle is inside the beam, and if so, calculating a factor. This factor will dictate changes to the particle\'s brightness, size, and color, giving them a more vibrant feel.\n\n\n"
