  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Cursor Control**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the implications of disabling cursor tracking. The goal is to anchor the light beam at a fixed diagonal, removing any dependence on pointer movement. This feels like it will simplify user interaction and behavior significantly. I\'m focusing on the technical steps to remove the listener and maintain the specified angle, while keeping the other features.\n\n\n**Implementing Particle Effects**\n\nI\'m now focused on particle implementation within `VolumetricLightBeam.tsx`. I\'m starting with initializing an array of particles, setting up data for their `x`, `y`, radius, speed, and base alpha properties. The plan is to have a gentle upward drift with faint horizontal movement, and to make the particles react subtly when they intersect the light beam by increasing brightness and giving them a cyan glint. I\'m aiming for an organic, starry effect.\n\n\n**Refining Particle Twinkle**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the particle effects in `VolumetricLightBeam.tsx`. The goal is to achieve a nice starry background. I\'ve introduced `twinkleFreq`, `twinklePhase`, and `driftPhase` to vary the twinkle behavior. The particles now drift, wrap around the screen edges, and the light beam renders with a fixed angle. The subtle breathing effect with slight variations in the angle and intensity is now working. I\'ve eliminated mouse tracking entirely.\n\n\n**Calculating Beam Interactions**\n\nI\'m now calculating particle interactions with the light beam, taking time into consideration. I\'m focusing on converting the particle\'s normalized `x` and `y` coordinates to canvas coordinates (`px`, `py`). I then check if each particle is within the light beam\'s parameters using `dist`, `pAngle`, and the `angle` of the beam. I\'m using `beamHalfSpread` for determining if the particle is in the beam. I\'m computing a `inBeam` lighting factor based on `lateralFactor` and `distFactor`. Outside the beam, the particle simply twinkles, affecting its alpha.\n\n\n**Enhancing Particle Rendering**\n\nI\'m now integrating the color and interaction logic. The particles are silvery-white, using `rgba(225, 235, 255, ${alpha})`. Inside the beam, the alpha increases, creating a catch-the-light effect, using `Math.min(1.0, (p.baseAlpha + inBeam * 0.75 * intensity) * twinkle)`. I\'m adding a cyan glint with a soft aura based on the `inBeam` value, using global composite operation \'screen\' for visual effect. The particle cores interpolate towards cyan/white, making them light up when in the beam.\n\n\n**Removing Unnecessary Hints**\n\nI\'ve removed the bottom instruction bar, streamlining the interface. Now, I\'m verifying the effects on the user experience. The particles still drift gently and react subtly with the beam, maintaining a starry, organic appearance. I\'m satisfied with the visual clarity.\n\n\n**Refining UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI. I\'ve removed the bottom instruction bar. I\'m verifying the changes to remove cursor sway references in the hero description, specs callout, and inspector. I\'m replacing \"Damped Parallax\" with \"Fixed Diagonal Projection\" and updating the specs description in the details modal. The cursor sway sensitivity slider has been removed from the inspector. I\'m considering a \"Star Dust Particles\" toggle or density slider in the inspector for user control.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_558377"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React, { useEffect, useRef } from \'react\';\\n\\nexport interface VolumetricLightBeamProps {\\n  /** Mode: \'dark\' (default cosmic beam) or \'illuminated\' (boosted radiant beam) */\\n  isIlluminated?: boolean;\\n  /** Primary core color (e.g. electric cyan #00f2fe) */\\n  coreColor?: string;\\n  /** Secondary gradient color (e.g. neon violet/purple #8a2be2) */\\n  secondaryColor?: string;\\n  /** Base canvas solid background color (default #0b0d19) */\\n  backgroundColor?: string;\\n  /** Multiplier for overall beam brightness/opacity (default 1.0) */\\n  intensityMultiplier?: number;\\n  /** Beam cone spread in degrees (default ~42\302\260) */\\n  spreadAngleDeg?: number;\\n  /** Whether idle breathing motion is active (default true) */\\n  idleMotion?: boolean;\\n  /** Whether floating star/dust particles are rendered (default true) */\\n  showParticles?: boolean;\\n  /** Optional custom origin coordinates {x, y} in pixels. If omitted, uses top-right anchor */\\n  originOverride?: { x: number; y: number } | null;\\n  /** Callback notifying parent of the calculated light origin {x, y} */\\n  onOriginUpdate?: (origin: { x: number; y: number }) => void;\\n  /** Custom class name for container */\\n  className?: string;\\n}\\n\\ninterface StarParticle {\\n  x: number;          // 0 to 1 normalized\\n  y: number;          // 0 to 1 normalized\\n  radius: number;     // pixel radius (subtle, 0.6 - 1.8px)\\n  speedY: number;     // slow upward drift\\n  speedX: number;     // gentle horizontal drift\\n  baseAlpha: number;  // 0.15 - 0.45\\n  twinkleFreq: number;// oscillation speed\\n  twinklePhase: number;\\n  driftPhase: number;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * VolumetricLightBeam\\n * \\n * High-performance, velvety smooth volumetric spotlight component.\\n * - Fixed natural diagonal angle (top-right to bottom-left) without cursor tracking.\\n * - Subtle, slow idle breathing/undulating animation.\\n * - Floating starry dust particles drifting upward, catching soft cyan glints inside the beam.\\n */\\nexport const VolumetricLightBeam: React.FC<VolumetricLightBeamProps> = ({\\n  isIlluminated = false,\\n  coreColor = \'#00f2fe\',\\n  secondaryColor = \'#8a2be2\',\\n  backgroundColor = \'#0b0d19\',\\n  intensityMultiplier = 1.0,\\n  spreadAngleDeg = 42,\\n  idleMotion = true,\\n  showParticles = true,\\n  originOverride = null,\\n  onOriginUpdate,\\n  className = \'\',\\n}) => {\\n  const canvasRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n  const animFrameRef = useRef<number | null>(null);\\n\\n  // Dynamic state tracked for smooth breathing and physics\\n  const stateRef = useRef({\\n    currentIntensity: isIlluminated ? 1.4 : 0.95,\\n    targetIntensity: isIlluminated ? 1.4 : 0.95,\\n    currentSpread: (spreadAngleDeg * Math.PI) / 180,\\n    targetSpread: (spreadAngleDeg * Math.PI) / 180,\\n    originX: 0,\\n    originY: 0,\\n    startTime: performance.now(),\\n    particles: [] as StarParticle[],\\n  });\\n\\n  // Initialize scattered, organic floating star/dot particles\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const particleCount = 95;\\n    const particles: StarParticle[] = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < particleCount; i++) {\\n      particles.push({\\n        x: Math.random(),\\n        y: Math.random(),\\n        radius: 0.6 + Math.random() * 1.2,\\n        speedY: -(0.00014 + Math.random() * 0.00032), // gentle upward float\\n        speedX: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.0001,       // ambient drift\\n        baseAlpha: 0.14 + Math.random() * 0.32,\\n        twinkleFreq: 1.0 + Math.random() * 2.2,\\n        twinklePhase: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\\n        driftPhase: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    stateRef.current.particles = particles;\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Keep target spread & intensity updated when props change\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    stateRef.current.targetIntensity = (isIlluminated ? 1.4 : 0.95) * intensityMultiplier;\\n    stateRef.current.targetSpread = (spreadAngleDeg * Math.PI) / 180;\\n  }, [isIlluminated, intensityMultiplier, spreadAngleDeg]);\\n\\n  // Sync CSS custom properties on document element for smooth glassmorphism / ambient transitions\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const root = document.documentElement;\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-intensity\', String(isIlluminated ? 1.4 * intensityMultiplier : 0.95 * intensityMultiplier));\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-core-color\', coreColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-secondary-color\', secondaryColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--bg-navy\', backgroundColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--illuminate-state\', isIlluminated ? \'illuminated\' : \'dark\');\\n  }, [isIlluminated, coreColor, secondaryColor, backgroundColor, intensityMultiplier]);\\n\\n  // Main high-performance render loop\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false });\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    let dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n\\n    const resize = () => {\\n      dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n      const width = window.innerWidth;\\n      const height = window.innerHeight;\\n\\n      canvas.width = Math.floor(width * dpr);\\n      canvas.height = Math.floor(height * dpr);\\n      canvas.style.width = `${width}px`;\\n      canvas.style.height = `${height}px`;\\n\\n      // Origin point: near the top-right corner where the illuminate switch sits\\n      const defaultOriginX = width - Math.max(64, width * 0.055);\\n      const defaultOriginY = Math.max(48, height * 0.055);\\n\\n      const ox = originOverride ? originOverride.x : defaultOriginX;\\n      const oy = originOverride ? originOverride.y : defaultOriginY;\\n\\n      stateRef.current.originX = ox;\\n      stateRef.current.originY = oy;\\n\\n      if (onOriginUpdate) {\\n        onOriginUpdate({ x: ox, y: oy });\\n      }\\n    };\\n\\n    resize();\\n    window.addEventListener(\'resize\', resize, { passive: true });\\n\\n    // Render step\\n    const render = (now: number) => {\\n      const state = stateRef.current;\\n      const time = (now - state.startTime) * 0.001;\\n      const width = canvas.width / dpr;\\n      const height = canvas.height / dpr;\\n\\n      // 1. Fixed natural diagonal base angle from top-right origin toward bottom-left (no cursor tracking)\\n      const targetPointX = width * 0.12;\\n      const targetPointY = height * 0.88;\\n      const baseAngle = Math.atan2(targetPointY - state.originY, targetPointX - state.originX);\\n\\n      // 2. Subtle, slow idle breathing/undulating animation\\n      const idleAngleDrift = idleMotion ? Math.sin(time * 0.5) * 0.018 : 0;\\n      const idleBreathingIntensity = idleMotion ? Math.sin(time * 0.8) * 0.05 : 0;\\n      const idleSpreadDrift = idleMotion ? Math.cos(time * 0.6) * 0.02 : 0;\\n\\n      const angle = baseAngle + idleAngleDrift;\\n\\n      // Smooth dampening for intensity & spread adjustments\\n      state.currentIntensity += (state.targetIntensity - state.currentIntensity) * 0.08;\\n      state.currentSpread += (state.targetSpread - state.currentSpread) * 0.06;\\n\\n      const intensity = Math.max(0.05, state.currentIntensity * (1 + idleBreathingIntensity));\\n      const spread = Math.max(0.1, state.currentSpread + idleSpreadDrift);\\n      const halfSpread = spread / 2;\\n\\n      // Setup drawing transform for HiDPI\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\\n\\n      // 3. Solid velvety base background (deep midnight navy #0b0d19)\\n      if (isIlluminated) {\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#0e1122\';\\n      } else {\\n        ctx.fillStyle = backgroundColor;\\n      }\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\\n\\n      const ox = state.originX;\\n      const oy = state.originY;\\n      const reach = Math.hypot(width, height) * 1.45;\\n\\n      // Helper to draw a cone polygon sector\\n      const drawConePath = (coneHalfAngle: number) => {\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(ox, oy);\\n        const steps = 18;\\n        const startA = angle - coneHalfAngle;\\n        const endA = angle + coneHalfAngle;\\n        for (let i = 0; i <= steps; i++) {\\n          const a = startA + (endA - startA) * (i / steps);\\n          const px = ox + Math.cos(a) * reach;\\n          const py = oy + Math.sin(a) * reach;\\n          ctx.lineTo(px, py);\\n        }\\n        ctx.closePath();\\n      };\\n\\n      // PASS 1: Broad Velvety Ambient Fog / Bloom (Heavy Blur, soft atmospheric falloff)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(64px)\';\\n      }\\n      drawConePath(halfSpread * 1.6);\\n      const gradAmbient = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 10, ox, oy, reach * 0.95);\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(0.0, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.32 * intensity));\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(0.35, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.22 * intensity));\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(0.70, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.08 * intensity));\\n      gradAmbient.addColorStop(1.0, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradAmbient;\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 2: Main Volumetric Spotlight Body (Medium Blur, vibrant Electric Cyan into Neon Violet)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(30px)\';\\n      }\\n      drawConePath(halfSpread);\\n      const gradMain = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 5, ox, oy, reach * 0.85);\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.88 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.12, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.72 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.32, hexToRgba(\'#4f46e5\', 0.58 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.55, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.42 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(0.80, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.14 * intensity));\\n      gradMain.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradMain;\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 3: Core Intense Concentrated Beam (Tighter angle, luminous highlight)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(14px)\';\\n      }\\n      drawConePath(halfSpread * 0.45);\\n      const gradCore = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 0, ox, oy, reach * 0.65);\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(\'#ffffff\', 0.95 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.10, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.85 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.35, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.45 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(0.65, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.20 * intensity));\\n      gradCore.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradCore;\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 4: Stage Light Aperture / Emitter Glow (Point of origin near toggle switch)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(22px)\';\\n      }\\n      const apertureGlow = ctx.createRadialGradient(ox, oy, 0, ox, oy, Math.min(220, width * 0.28));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(\'#ffffff\', 0.98 * intensity));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(0.15, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.75 * intensity));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(0.45, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.35 * intensity));\\n      apertureGlow.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = apertureGlow;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(ox, oy, Math.min(220, width * 0.28), 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 5: Soft Atmospheric Floor Bounce (Bottom-Left Corner Wash)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(80px)\';\\n      }\\n      const bounceX = width * 0.12;\\n      const bounceY = height * 0.88;\\n      const bounceRad = Math.min(380, width * 0.38);\\n      const bounceGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(bounceX, bounceY, 0, bounceX, bounceY, bounceRad);\\n      bounceGrad.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.22 * intensity));\\n      bounceGrad.addColorStop(0.40, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.10 * intensity));\\n      bounceGrad.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = bounceGrad;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(bounceX, bounceY, bounceRad, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 6: Floating Star / Dust Particles\\n      // - Scattered, faint twinkling stars drifting slowly upward\\n      // - Catching the light inside the cyan/purple beam with boosted brightness & soft cyan glint\\n      if (showParticles && state.particles.length > 0) {\\n        const particles = state.particles;\\n        const beamConeHalfAngle = halfSpread * 1.18;\\n\\n        for (let i = 0; i < particles.length; i++) {\\n          const p = particles[i];\\n\\n          // Slow upward float and gentle ambient wave\\n          p.y += p.speedY;\\n          p.x += p.speedX + Math.sin(time * 0.45 + p.driftPhase) * 0.0001;\\n\\n          // Wrap boundaries organically\\n          if (p.y < -0.02) {\\n            p.y = 1.02;\\n            p.x = Math.random();\\n          }\\n          if (p.x < -0.02) p.x = 1.02;\\n          if (p.x > 1.02) p.x = -0.02;\\n\\n          const px = p.x * width;\\n          const py = p.y * height;\\n\\n          // Calculate angle and distance from beam origin\\n          const dx = px - ox;\\n          const dy = py - oy;\\n          const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\\n          const pAngle = Math.atan2(dy, dx);\\n\\n          // Angular difference relative to beam direction\\n          let diff = pAngle - angle;\\n          while (diff > Math.PI) diff -= Math.PI * 2;\\n          while (diff < -Math.PI) diff += Math.PI * 2;\\n          const absDiff = Math.abs(diff);\\n\\n          // Determine if particle is inside the beam\\n          let inBeam = 0;\\n          if (absDiff < beamConeHalfAngle && dist < reach * 0.95) {\\n            const lateral = 1 - absDiff / beamConeHalfAngle;\\n            const longitudinal = Math.max(0, 1 - dist / (reach * 0.95));\\n            inBeam = Math.pow(lateral, 1.2) * (0.35 + 0.65 * longitudinal);\\n          }\\n\\n          // Twinkle oscillation\\n          const twinkle = 0.72 + 0.28 * Math.sin(time * p.twinkleFreq + p.twinklePhase);\\n\\n          if (inBeam > 0.05) {\\n            // Particle catches the light inside the beam\\n            const beamBoost = inBeam * 0.65 * intensity;\\n            const alpha = Math.min(1.0, (p.baseAlpha + beamBoost) * twinkle);\\n            const renderedRadius = p.radius * (1 + inBeam * 0.35);\\n\\n            // Soft cyan glint aura\\n            ctx.save();\\n            ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n            ctx.fillStyle = hexToRgba(coreColor, inBeam * 0.32 * intensity);\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.arc(px, py, renderedRadius * 2.6, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n            ctx.fill();\\n\\n            // Bright sparkling core catching light\\n            ctx.fillStyle = inBeam > 0.4 ? hexToRgba(\'#e0fcff\', alpha) : hexToRgba(coreColor, alpha);\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.arc(px, py, renderedRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n            ctx.fill();\\n            ctx.restore();\\n          } else {\\n            // Faint ambient star twinkling outside the beam\\n            const alpha = p.baseAlpha * twinkle;\\n            ctx.save();\\n            ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(215, 230, 255, ${alpha.toFixed(3)})`;\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.arc(px, py, p.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n            ctx.fill();\\n            ctx.restore();\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      animFrameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(render);\\n    };\\n\\n    animFrameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(render);\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'resize\', resize);\\n      if (animFrameRef.current) {\\n        cancelAnimationFrame(animFrameRef.current);\\n      }\\n    };\\n  }, [coreColor, secondaryColor, backgroundColor, idleMotion, showParticles, originOverride, onOriginUpdate, isIlluminated]);\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className={`fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none select-none overflow-hidden ${className}`}>\\n      <canvas\\n        ref={canvasRef}\\n        className=\\\"absolute inset-0 block w-full h-full\\\"\\n        style={{\\n          backgroundColor,\\n          mixBlendMode: \'normal\',\\n        }}\\n      />\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\\n\\n/**\\n * Utility helper to convert hex to rgba string\\n */\\nfunction hexToRgba(hex: string, alpha: number): string {\\n  let c = hex.trim();\\n  if (c.startsWith(\'#\')) {\\n    c = c.slice(1);\\n  }\\n  if (c.length === 3) {\\n    c = c.split(\'\').map((char) => char + char).join(\'\');\\n  }\\n  const num = parseInt(c, 16);\\n  if (isNaN(num)) {\\n    return `rgba(0, 242, 254, ${alpha})`;\\n  }\\n  const r = (num >> 16) & 255;\\n  const g = (num >> 8) & 255;\\n  const b = num & 255;\\n  return `rgba(${r}, ${g}, ${b}, ${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, alpha))})`;\\n}\\n\\nexport default VolumetricLightBeam;\\n\",\"Description\":\"Update VolumetricLightBeam: disable cursor tracking listener, add subtle slow idle breathing, add organic floating twinkling starry dust particles with beam glinting\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/VolumetricLightBeam.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing updated component\",\"toolSummary\":\"Update VolumetricLightBeam component\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
