  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User Input**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user request, focusing on the specific adjustments. The key seems to be precise positioning of the light source. Currently, I\'m examining \"position the light source exactly in the center\" and exploring the possible implications to ensure an effective response.\n\n\n**Refining the Visualization**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual implementation, starting with precise CSS for the central glow. I\'m imagining an elliptical core with an electric cyan to vibrant neon purple gradient that smoothly blends into the deep navy background. I\342\200\231m thinking to add the toggle there too. I am exploring the use of scaling and distortion effects to make the motion more lively.\n\n\n**Amplifying Cosmic Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dynamic aspects. My objective is a dead-center nebula core with pronounced motion. I\'m aiming for fluid rotation, wave ripples, pulsing breathing from 0.9x to 1.25x scale, and accelerated particle motion with bright glints. The central light source is clear now. I\'m breaking down the specifications for each requested element of the effect.\n\n\n**Integrating the Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating the control switch with the visuals. I plan to position the \"Illuminate\" toggle right in the center, maybe above the central glow to serve as the power switch. I want it to be a prominent element of the composition, keeping the top bar clean. Furthermore, I\'m focusing on making the motion dynamic, but not overly static.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'ve calculated the breathing scale effects for the central glow now. My focus is on achieving a clear and noticeable dynamic motion. I\'ve designed the motion so that it oscillates between roughly 0.88x and 1.26x. I am aiming for distinct rhythmic breathing effects to accentuate its presence.\n\n\n**Enhancing Dynamic Motion**\n\nI\'m now optimizing the dynamic motion effects for the central nebula. I\'m focusing on layered, rotating elliptical lobes or morphing petals for a living effect, using harmonic eccentricity and time-based rotation. I\'m also exploring a wave distortion using gradient modulation or bezier curves for a swirling, rippling aurora. I\'m boosting particle motion to emphasize the vortex, with faster speeds and distinct cyan/magenta glints and trails.\n\n\n**Constructing Layered Effects**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the code for `VolumetricLightBeam.tsx` to build the cosmic core. I\'m focusing on a multi-layer approach for that core, with precise formulas for scale, position and radii. I am refining the intensity and pulse scale to build the pulsing effect. I\'m crafting the layers of ambient washes, gradients and primary lobes.\n\n\n**Implementing Layered Rotation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the layered, rotating elliptical lobes into the central core. I\'ve defined the rotation angles (`angleA`, `angleB`), eccentricities (`scaleX`, `scaleY`), and blur parameters. The core layers will use specific colors and transparency, providing a complex, pulsating effect. I\'m focusing on electric cyan to vibrant neon purple gradients.\n\n\n**Refining Inner Core**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the high-energy nucleus of the core. I\'ve defined a small, intense, pulsating core with a radiant white center, transitioning into electric cyan, to deliver the pulsing and undulating effects. Furthermore, I am implementing distinct floating star/dot particles with boosted orbital and drift velocities, with a visible upward drift. I\'m focusing on the effect of the particle dynamics to ensure the core is visually active.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1890406"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React, { useEffect, useRef } from \'react\';\\n\\nexport interface VolumetricLightBeamProps {\\n  /** Mode: \'dark\' (default cosmic beam) or \'illuminated\' (boosted radiant beam) */\\n  isIlluminated?: boolean;\\n  /** Primary core color (default: electric cyan #00f2fe) */\\n  coreColor?: string;\\n  /** Secondary gradient color (default: neon violet/purple #8a2be2) */\\n  secondaryColor?: string;\\n  /** Base canvas solid background color (default #0b0d19) */\\n  backgroundColor?: string;\\n  /** Multiplier for overall beam brightness/opacity (default 1.0) */\\n  intensityMultiplier?: number;\\n  /** Whether dynamic fluid motion & pulsing is active (default true) */\\n  dynamicMotion?: boolean;\\n  /** Whether floating star/dust particles are rendered (default true) */\\n  showParticles?: boolean;\\n  /** Custom class name for container */\\n  className?: string;\\n}\\n\\ninterface StarParticle {\\n  x: number;          // 0 to 1 normalized\\n  y: number;          // 0 to 1 normalized\\n  radius: number;     // pixel radius (0.8 - 2.2px)\\n  speedY: number;     // boosted upward drift velocity\\n  speedX: number;     // horizontal drift\\n  swirlAngle: number; // orbital angle around center\\n  swirlSpeed: number; // angular speed\\n  baseAlpha: number;  // 0.18 - 0.55\\n  twinkleFreq: number;// oscillation speed\\n  twinklePhase: number;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * VolumetricLightBeam\\n * \\n * Exact Center Radial Glowing Core with Amplified Fluid Motion:\\n * - Positioned at exact dead center of the viewport (50% X, 50% Y).\\n * - Rich, radial/elliptical glowing core emanating outward into #0b0d19 navy-black.\\n * - Electric cyan (#00f2fe) core blending into vibrant neon violet (#8a2be2), fading before edges.\\n * - Amplified rhythmic breathing/pulsing scale (0.9x to 1.25x).\\n * - Morphing multi-harmonic wave ripples and dual-rotating fluid elliptical lobes.\\n * - Boosted particle motion speed with bright cyan/violet glints through the central glow.\\n */\\nexport const VolumetricLightBeam: React.FC<VolumetricLightBeamProps> = ({\\n  isIlluminated = false,\\n  coreColor = \'#00f2fe\',\\n  secondaryColor = \'#8a2be2\',\\n  backgroundColor = \'#0b0d19\',\\n  intensityMultiplier = 1.0,\\n  dynamicMotion = true,\\n  showParticles = true,\\n  className = \'\',\\n}) => {\\n  const canvasRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n  const animFrameRef = useRef<number | null>(null);\\n\\n  // Dynamic state tracked for smooth transition between illuminated & dark\\n  const stateRef = useRef({\\n    currentIntensity: isIlluminated ? 1.5 : 1.05,\\n    targetIntensity: isIlluminated ? 1.5 : 1.05,\\n    startTime: performance.now(),\\n    particles: [] as StarParticle[],\\n  });\\n\\n  // Initialize scattered, organic floating star/dot particles with boosted velocity\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const particleCount = 110;\\n    const particles: StarParticle[] = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < particleCount; i++) {\\n      particles.push({\\n        x: Math.random(),\\n        y: Math.random(),\\n        radius: 0.8 + Math.random() * 1.4,\\n        speedY: -(0.00045 + Math.random() * 0.00095), // boosted noticeable upward speed\\n        speedX: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.00035,\\n        swirlAngle: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\\n        swirlSpeed: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.008,\\n        baseAlpha: 0.18 + Math.random() * 0.38,\\n        twinkleFreq: 1.6 + Math.random() * 3.0,\\n        twinklePhase: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    stateRef.current.particles = particles;\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Update target intensity when mode changes\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    stateRef.current.targetIntensity = (isIlluminated ? 1.55 : 1.05) * intensityMultiplier;\\n  }, [isIlluminated, intensityMultiplier]);\\n\\n  // Sync CSS custom properties for ambient illumination\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const root = document.documentElement;\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-intensity\', String(isIlluminated ? 1.55 * intensityMultiplier : 1.05 * intensityMultiplier));\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-core-color\', coreColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--beam-secondary-color\', secondaryColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--bg-navy\', backgroundColor);\\n    root.style.setProperty(\'--illuminate-state\', isIlluminated ? \'illuminated\' : \'dark\');\\n  }, [isIlluminated, coreColor, secondaryColor, backgroundColor, intensityMultiplier]);\\n\\n  // Main high-performance render loop\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext(\'2d\', { alpha: false });\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    let dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n\\n    const resize = () => {\\n      dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n      const width = window.innerWidth;\\n      const height = window.innerHeight;\\n\\n      canvas.width = Math.floor(width * dpr);\\n      canvas.height = Math.floor(height * dpr);\\n      canvas.style.width = `${width}px`;\\n      canvas.style.height = `${height}px`;\\n    };\\n\\n    resize();\\n    window.addEventListener(\'resize\', resize, { passive: true });\\n\\n    // Render step\\n    const render = (now: number) => {\\n      const state = stateRef.current;\\n      const time = (now - state.startTime) * 0.001;\\n      const width = canvas.width / dpr;\\n      const height = canvas.height / dpr;\\n\\n      // Smooth dampening for intensity\\n      state.currentIntensity += (state.targetIntensity - state.currentIntensity) * 0.08;\\n\\n      // 1. Amplified Rhythmic Breathing / Pulsing Scale Effect\\n      // Scales rhythmically between ~0.90x and ~1.25x with dual harmonics\\n      const pulseScale = dynamicMotion\\n        ? 1.0 + Math.sin(time * 1.7) * 0.16 + Math.sin(time * 0.85) * 0.08\\n        : 1.0;\\n\\n      const intensityPulse = dynamicMotion\\n        ? 1.0 + Math.sin(time * 2.2) * 0.12\\n        : 1.0;\\n\\n      const intensity = Math.max(0.05, state.currentIntensity * intensityPulse);\\n\\n      // Exact Dead Center\\n      const cx = width / 2;\\n      const cy = height / 2;\\n\\n      // Maximum reach: bound so it gracefully fades to 0 before hitting outer viewport borders\\n      const minDim = Math.min(width, height);\\n      const baseRadius = minDim * 0.52 * pulseScale;\\n\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\\n\\n      // 2. Base Solid Midnight Navy (#0b0d19)\\n      if (isIlluminated) {\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#0f1228\';\\n      } else {\\n        ctx.fillStyle = backgroundColor;\\n      }\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\\n\\n      // PASS 1: Broad Velvety Ambient Violet Aura (Heavy Blur, soft outer falloff)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(65px)\';\\n      }\\n      const auraRadius = baseRadius * 1.35;\\n      const gradAura = ctx.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, 10, cx, cy, auraRadius);\\n      gradAura.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.38 * intensity));\\n      gradAura.addColorStop(0.40, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.22 * intensity));\\n      gradAura.addColorStop(0.72, hexToRgba(\'#311042\', 0.10 * intensity));\\n      gradAura.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradAura;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(cx, cy, auraRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 2: Primary Rotating Elliptical Lobe A (Fluid clockwise rotation & morphing)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(34px)\';\\n      }\\n      ctx.translate(cx, cy);\\n      const rotAngleA = dynamicMotion ? time * 0.38 : 0;\\n      ctx.rotate(rotAngleA);\\n      const scaleXA = dynamicMotion ? 1.18 + Math.sin(time * 1.3) * 0.16 : 1.15;\\n      const scaleYA = dynamicMotion ? 0.88 + Math.cos(time * 1.5) * 0.14 : 0.90;\\n      ctx.scale(scaleXA, scaleYA);\\n\\n      const gradLobeA = ctx.createRadialGradient(0, 0, 5, 0, 0, baseRadius * 0.92);\\n      gradLobeA.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.92 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeA.addColorStop(0.18, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.72 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeA.addColorStop(0.42, hexToRgba(\'#4f46e5\', 0.55 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeA.addColorStop(0.68, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.38 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeA.addColorStop(0.92, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.08 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeA.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradLobeA;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(0, 0, baseRadius * 0.92, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 3: Secondary Counter-Rotating Elliptical Lobe B (Morphing diagonal counter-flow)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(28px)\';\\n      }\\n      ctx.translate(cx, cy);\\n      const rotAngleB = dynamicMotion ? -time * 0.28 : -0.5;\\n      ctx.rotate(rotAngleB);\\n      const scaleXB = dynamicMotion ? 0.86 + Math.cos(time * 1.6) * 0.15 : 0.88;\\n      const scaleYB = dynamicMotion ? 1.20 + Math.sin(time * 1.2) * 0.18 : 1.15;\\n      ctx.scale(scaleXB, scaleYB);\\n\\n      const gradLobeB = ctx.createRadialGradient(0, 0, 5, 0, 0, baseRadius * 0.84);\\n      gradLobeB.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.85 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeB.addColorStop(0.24, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.55 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeB.addColorStop(0.52, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.42 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeB.addColorStop(0.85, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.12 * intensity));\\n      gradLobeB.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradLobeB;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(0, 0, baseRadius * 0.84, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 4: Dynamic Fluid Wave Ripple (Organic undulating multi-harmonic contour)\\n      // Visibly ripples, breathes, and morphs over time\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(18px)\';\\n      }\\n      ctx.translate(cx, cy);\\n\\n      const waveSteps = 48;\\n      const waveRadius = baseRadius * 0.65;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      for (let i = 0; i <= waveSteps; i++) {\\n        const theta = (i / waveSteps) * Math.PI * 2;\\n        // 3rd & 5th harmonic wave distortion creating liquid flowing ripples\\n        const ripple = dynamicMotion\\n          ? Math.sin(theta * 3 + time * 2.2) * 0.14 +\\n            Math.cos(theta * 5 - time * 1.6) * 0.10 +\\n            Math.sin(theta * 2 + time * 3.1) * 0.08\\n          : 0;\\n        const r = waveRadius * (1 + ripple);\\n        const px = Math.cos(theta) * r;\\n        const py = Math.sin(theta) * r;\\n        if (i === 0) {\\n          ctx.moveTo(px, py);\\n        } else {\\n          ctx.lineTo(px, py);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      ctx.closePath();\\n\\n      const gradRipple = ctx.createRadialGradient(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, waveRadius * 1.15);\\n      gradRipple.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(\'#ffffff\', 0.98 * intensity));\\n      gradRipple.addColorStop(0.12, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.90 * intensity));\\n      gradRipple.addColorStop(0.38, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.58 * intensity));\\n      gradRipple.addColorStop(0.70, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.32 * intensity));\\n      gradRipple.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradRipple;\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 5: Radiant Luminous Central Core Nucleus (White-hot cyan center)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n      if (\'filter\' in ctx) {\\n        ctx.filter = \'blur(12px)\';\\n      }\\n      const nucleusRadius = Math.min(85, minDim * 0.16) * pulseScale;\\n      const gradNucleus = ctx.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, 0, cx, cy, nucleusRadius);\\n      gradNucleus.addColorStop(0.00, hexToRgba(\'#ffffff\', 1.0 * intensity));\\n      gradNucleus.addColorStop(0.20, hexToRgba(\'#e0ffff\', 0.95 * intensity));\\n      gradNucleus.addColorStop(0.50, hexToRgba(coreColor, 0.75 * intensity));\\n      gradNucleus.addColorStop(0.82, hexToRgba(secondaryColor, 0.30 * intensity));\\n      gradNucleus.addColorStop(1.00, \'rgba(11, 13, 25, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradNucleus;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(cx, cy, nucleusRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // PASS 6: Energized Floating Star / Dust Particles\\n      // - Boosted motion speed (2x-3x)\\n      // - Upward float with gentle orbital swirl\\n      // - Igniting with brilliant electric cyan / neon violet glints as they traverse the central glow\\n      if (showParticles && state.particles.length > 0) {\\n        const particles = state.particles;\\n        const glowOuterRadius = baseRadius * 1.1;\\n\\n        for (let i = 0; i < particles.length; i++) {\\n          const p = particles[i];\\n\\n          // Boosted upward velocity and organic drift\\n          p.y += p.speedY;\\n          p.x += p.speedX;\\n\\n          // Subtle orbital swirl toward/around center\\n          p.swirlAngle += p.swirlSpeed;\\n          p.x += Math.cos(p.swirlAngle) * 0.00015;\\n\\n          // Wrap boundaries smoothly\\n          if (p.y < -0.02) {\\n            p.y = 1.02;\\n            p.x = Math.random();\\n          }\\n          if (p.x < -0.02) p.x = 1.02;\\n          if (p.x > 1.02) p.x = -0.02;\\n\\n          const px = p.x * width;\\n          const py = p.y * height;\\n\\n          // Radial distance from exact center\\n          const distToCenter = Math.hypot(px - cx, py - cy);\\n\\n          // Calculate illumination factor inside the central glow\\n          let inGlow = 0;\\n          if (distToCenter < glowOuterRadius) {\\n            inGlow = Math.max(0, 1 - distToCenter / glowOuterRadius);\\n            // Non-linear power curve for dramatic central brilliance\\n            inGlow = Math.pow(inGlow, 1.25);\\n          }\\n\\n          // Twinkle frequency\\n          const twinkle = 0.70 + 0.30 * Math.sin(time * p.twinkleFreq + p.twinklePhase);\\n\\n          if (inGlow > 0.05) {\\n            // Particle catches the energized central glow!\\n            const glowBoost = inGlow * 0.85 * intensity;\\n            const alpha = Math.min(1.0, (p.baseAlpha + glowBoost) * twinkle);\\n            const renderedRadius = p.radius * (1 + inGlow * 0.55);\\n\\n            // Radiant glint aura\\n            ctx.save();\\n            ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \'screen\';\\n            ctx.fillStyle = hexToRgba(coreColor, inGlow * 0.45 * intensity);\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.arc(px, py, renderedRadius * 3.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n            ctx.fill();\\n\\n            // Brilliant luminous star core\\n            ctx.fillStyle = inGlow > 0.45 ? hexToRgba(\'#ffffff\', alpha) : hexToRgba(coreColor, alpha);\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.arc(px, py, renderedRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n            ctx.fill();\\n            ctx.restore();\\n          } else {\\n            // Faint starry dust twinkling in outer velvet navy\\n            const alpha = p.baseAlpha * twinkle;\\n            ctx.save();\\n            ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(215, 230, 255, ${alpha.toFixed(3)})`;\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.arc(px, py, p.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n            ctx.fill();\\n            ctx.restore();\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      animFrameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(render);\\n    };\\n\\n    animFrameRef.current = requestAnimationFrame(render);\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'resize\', resize);\\n      if (animFrameRef.current) {\\n        cancelAnimationFrame(animFrameRef.current);\\n      }\\n    };\\n  }, [coreColor, secondaryColor, backgroundColor, dynamicMotion, showParticles, isIlluminated]);\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className={`fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none select-none overflow-hidden ${className}`}>\\n      <canvas\\n        ref={canvasRef}\\n        className=\\\"absolute inset-0 block w-full h-full\\\"\\n        style={{\\n          backgroundColor,\\n          mixBlendMode: \'normal\',\\n        }}\\n      />\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\\n\\n/**\\n * Utility helper to convert hex to rgba string\\n */\\nfunction hexToRgba(hex: string, alpha: number): string {\\n  let c = hex.trim();\\n  if (c.startsWith(\'#\')) {\\n    c = c.slice(1);\\n  }\\n  if (c.length === 3) {\\n    c = c.split(\'\').map((char) => char + char).join(\'\');\\n  }\\n  const num = parseInt(c, 16);\\n  if (isNaN(num)) {\\n    return `rgba(0, 242, 254, ${alpha})`;\\n  }\\n  const r = (num >> 16) & 255;\\n  const g = (num >> 8) & 255;\\n  const b = num & 255;\\n  return `rgba(${r}, ${g}, ${b}, ${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, alpha))})`;\\n}\\n\\nexport default VolumetricLightBeam;\\n\",\"Description\":\"Implement centered radial glowing core with amplified dynamic motion, fluid wave rippling, rotating lobes, and boosted particle motion\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/VolumetricLightBeam.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing component file\",\"toolSummary\":\"Update VolumetricLightBeam component for center radial glow\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
